  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas expands isothermally from a volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and then compressed to original volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> adiabatically. The initial pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and final pressure is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>. The total work done is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi></math>. Then:"
  },
