  "solution": {
    "text": "From the graph it is clear that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> .<br />Since the area under adiabatic process <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is greater than that of the isothermal process <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> . Therefore net word done<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></msub><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0129_031ef6c1d9f7.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.07774in;height:1.70755in\" />"
  }
